Subject: [PATCH 01/10] tools: the suspension variant on emscripten, and a test
 under node that ends as its main ends, within a bound

The feature webcpp-suspend (jspi by default, asyncify composing JavaScript exceptions) and /webcpp//node-test, which webcpp.run, webcpp.run-fail and webcpp.example link on every target: the header webcpp/test/exit_status.hpp, and on emscripten the pre-js that fails a test whose main did not finish and stops one past its bound of 120 s. The fixture library node_test_demo pins each case's exact status. demo's native_only_compiles takes the support too, so that it still compiles native_only.cpp the same way as native_only, which the lint's database lists once.
